    {
      "id": "joshua-tree",
      "name": "Joshua Tree",
      "state": "CA",
      "lat": 33.8734,
      "lng": -115.9010,
      "visited": true,
      "visitDates": "Jul 26-28, 2024",
      "blurb": "I spent a weekend at Joshua Tree while I was interning at JPL. I hadn't really known what to expect — I'm not a climber, which is what the park is known for, but I love the desert, so I knew I'd have fun just looking at the scenery. Unfortunately, there was a major heat wave, and the rangers told me not to be hiking for around two hours before and after solar noon — that's a lot of the day! I made the most of it, though — I ended up staying up late at night to look at the stars, and during the day doing a bunch of short little hikes and loops and staying in the shade as much as possible. Truthfully, my favorite part was probably the World Famous Crochet Museum, a tiny little museum chock full of collected crochet pieces curated by an amazing artist named Shari Elf. I don't have any pictures of myself at the park (whoops) so here's a picture of some of the lovely little plushes on display.",
      "photo": "joshua-tree.jpg"
    },
