    {
      "id": "zion",
      "name": "Zion",
      "state": "UT",
      "lat": 37.2982,
      "lng": -113.0263,
      "visited": true,
      "visitDates": "Jul 24–26, 2026",
      "blurb": "The moment I read about the Narrows top-down hike, I knew that I just had to do it. I had a pretty limited time in the park, but the website said it could be done in one day, so I decided to give it a try. Wow! Not for the faint of heart. 15.7 miles in 12 hours, starting from a long shuttle bus that left at 6am, and if I missed the 8pm shuttle back to Watchman campground, it would've been another 7-mile hike back. I was a lot slower hiking in the river than I had accounted for, so I was pretty nervous about making it back in time. I made it with about 30 minutes to spare, but my feet fell like they were going to fall off by the end. The scenery was well worth it, though. It was so lush and green upriver. Probably the best (and hardest!) day hike I've ever done!",
      "photo": "zion.jpg"
    }
